// The C twin of tests/testlvalueopbind: in C an assignment yields a prvalue
// (C11 6.5.16p3), so `&(x = 3)` is a constraint violation. madc admits the
// C++ lvalue-yielding operators only in a C++ mode and keeps refusing this.
// Oracle: gcc -std=c17 "lvalue required as unary '&' operand"; clang -std=c17
// "cannot take the address of an rvalue of type 'int'".
int main(void)
{
	int x = 1;
	int *p = &(x = 3);
	return *p;
}
